cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project in your research or your own build, please cite it."
title: "Pothole Detection Lab: camera, sensor, and hybrid pothole detection with a real-world transfer study"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Stading"
    given-names: "Warren"
date-released: 2026-06-12
abstract: >
  A research platform for pothole detection that trains and fairly
  benchmarks image models (YOLOv8, Faster R-CNN, U-Net, ResNet18),
  motion-sensor models (Random Forest, 1D-CNN, BiLSTM), and hybrid
  fusion models, with a strict pothole-versus-other-anomaly task
  definition. Includes a 94-test benchmark and a pre-registered,
  blinded real-world transfer study on iPhone and nuScenes drives
  showing that the in-lab hybrid advantage does not survive platform
  transfer when one modality collapses.
keywords:
  - pothole detection
  - sensor fusion
  - domain transfer
  - autonomous vehicles
  - road maintenance
license: MIT
